cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this toolkit, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ohmsi-kit: Oral History Multi-Speaker Interpretation-Kit"
abstract: >-
  A toolkit that uses Whisper speech-to-text models and SpeechBrain
  diarization to turn oral history recordings into CSV transcripts of
  timestamped dialogue separated by speaker, with advanced scripts for
  difficult audio, and a local workspace for copy editing each transcript
  against its recording as it will appear on an Oral History as Data site.
authors:
  - family-names: Weymouth
    given-names: Andrew
repository-code: "https://github.com/Scholarly-Projects/ohmsi-kit"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - oral history
  - transcription
  - speaker diarization
  - Whisper
  - SpeechBrain
  - digital humanities
  - Oral History as Data
